<section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
        <h1>Research</h1>
        <p>
            I am interested in observational astronomy and planetary science, particularly the study of planetary surfaces through imaging, instrumentation, and computational analysis. As an undergraduate, I am building the scientific and technical foundation necessary to contribute to research in these areas through coursework, independent study, observational projects, and scientific software development. My current preparation for research includes undergraduate coursework in astronomy, mathematics, and physics, independent study of planetary science and observational techniques, continued astronomical observing, and development of scientific software related to astronomy.
        </p>
        <p>
            I hope to become involved in undergraduate research focused on planetary science or observational astronomy, particularly projects involving image analysis, remote sensing, or computational methods. In the long term, I hope to pursue graduate study and contribute to research that combines observational data, planetary science, and scientific computing.
        </p>
        
        <h2>Research Interests</h2>
        <h3> Planetary Science </h3>
        <p> 
            Understanding the formation and evolution of terrestrial planets, moons, and small bodies through comparative planetology and remote sensing.
        </p>
        
        <h3> Lunar Science </h3>
        <p> 
            Investigating lunar geology, impact cratering, volcanism, and surface evolution using telescopic observations and spacecraft data.
        </p>
        
        <h3> Solar Physics &amp; Observations </h3>
        <p> 
            Observing and analyzing solar activity, sunspots, prominences, and chromospheric features while learning techniques for solar imaging and data analysis.
        </p> 
        
        <h3> Astronomical Instrumentation </h3>
        <p> 
            Studying telescope systems, detectors, and observational techniques that enable precise astronomical measurements and data collection.
        </p>
            
        <h3> Scientific Computing </h3>
        <p> 
            Developing software and computational tools that support astronomical observations, data analysis, visualization, automation, and reproducible scientific workflows.
        </p>
        
        <h2>Research Projects</h2>
        <p>
            Research projects will be added here as they become part of my undergraduate work.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

